# Cloudflare Workers Assets ignore — files here are NOT uploaded.
# Cloudflare hard-caps any single asset at 25 MiB; ONE oversized file
# aborts the ENTIRE `wrangler deploy`, which is why production was
# frozen on a stale build for so long. Keep big/non-runtime files out
# of the upload (they still stay on disk locally).

# The minify backup written mid-deploy (build.mjs → .index.dev.html). It's the
# full ~12 MB un-minified SOURCE; restore() deletes it locally, but wrangler
# uploads whatever is present during the deploy window, so exclude it here to
# stop the raw source shipping to the CDN.
.index.dev.html

# Full data-export dumps — never needed by the deployed game.
assets/Exports/

# Marketing-site flood video that keeps getting dropped into the game's
# Backgrounds folder. 36 MB, unused by the game, and over the 25 MiB cap.
assets/background/Backgrounds/websitefloodvideo.mp4

# `assets/3d models/` is the raw-model STAGING folder — .glb sources keep getting
# dropped here (Battletable 32.9 MiB, Vendor market cash register 53.4 MiB, …) and
# any one over 25 MiB aborts the whole deploy. Big .glb models for the walkable
# Card Shop belong in the Supabase `models` Storage bucket (upload via the in-shop
# "🛠 Edit Shop" / "🏗️ Build" admin panels), NOT the Pages bundle — Cloudflare
# can't serve a file this large anyway. Ignore EVERY .glb in this folder; the PNG
# textures next to them (under the cap) still deploy normally. Files stay on disk.
# NOTE: also ignore .glb in SUBfolders (e.g. "3d models/posters/Birth Of Universe
# 1.glb" — 41.9 MiB) — the single-* pattern only matches direct children, so a
# model dropped into a subfolder slipped through and aborted the whole deploy.
assets/3d models/*.glb
assets/3d models/**/*.glb

# Belt-and-suspenders: ANY .glb anywhere in the bundle. Runtime 3D models are
# served from the Supabase `models` Storage bucket, never the Pages upload.
**/*.glb

# EXCEPTION: the default Card Shop binder model ships in the bundle (it's the
# fixture EVERY shop gets, so it can't depend on a per-owner Storage upload).
# 14.8 MiB — comfortably under Cloudflare's 25 MiB per-asset cap.
!assets/3d models/Binder table.glb

# EXCEPTION: the two Containment Lab characters (☣️ /src/biolab). Same reasoning
# as the binder table — they are FIXTURES, not per-owner uploads: every player
# who enters the airlock is the researcher and becomes the sentinel, so the
# suit-up cannot depend on a Storage bucket the player has never written to.
# 684 KiB + 738 KiB, two orders of magnitude under the cap; both were already
# recompressed (4 files → 2, 30 MB → 1.4 MB) before they got here.
!models/lab/researcher.glb
!models/lab/sentinel.glb

# EXCEPTION: the Cracking Yard's operator (🛢 /src/refinery). Same reasoning
# again — it is the yard's fixture character, not a per-owner upload, so the
# walk cycle cannot depend on a Storage bucket the player has never written
# to. 0.75 MB, packed from three 8 MB exports.
!models/refinery/guardian.glb

# EXCEPTION: the three trucks (🚛 Truck Yard, 🛢 Cracking Yard). Catalogue
# fixtures rather than per-owner uploads — every player sees the same rigs on
# the shop floor, and the tanker is the model every refinery parks — so a
# Storage bucket the player has never written to cannot serve them.
# 342 + 363 + 474 KiB, all far under the 25 MiB cap, packed down from 364 MB
# and ~9 million triangles by tools/glbprop.mjs.
!models/trucks/tanker.glb
!models/trucks/freight_box.glb
!models/trucks/freight_rig.glb

# EXCEPTION: the two farm rigs (🌾 Bulk Feed and 🐄 Livestock, added with those
# two cargo classes in the Truck Yard). Same reasoning as the three above —
# catalogue fixtures every player sees on the same shop floor, never per-owner
# uploads — and the same pipeline: tools/glbprop.mjs took 93.7 MB /
# 3,077,745 triangles and 94.9 MB / ~3M down to 0.86 MiB (14,496 tris) and
# 1.31 MiB, with 1024px WebP textures. Masters in
# assets-source/glb-masters/trucks/, never under public/.
# 🔴 A MODEL PATH IN rigs.data.js WITHOUT A LINE HERE IS THE WORST FAILURE SHAPE
#   THIS FILE HAS: the blanket rule above means it works perfectly in local dev
#   and 404s only in production. Add the rig row and this line together.
!models/trucks/feed_truck.glb
!models/trucks/livestock_truck.glb

# EXCEPTION (v121v110): the white flatbed semi every FREIGHT rig now shows in
# the Truck Yard and drives in the Highway Haul, and the two shipping
# containers that ride on its deck there. Same pipeline (tools/glbprop.mjs):
# 26.7 MB → 0.84 MiB, 19.9 MB → 0.59 MiB, 16.7 MB → 0.53 MiB. Masters in
# assets-source/glb-masters/{trucks,containers}/.
!models/trucks/freight_semi.glb
!models/trucks/freight_semi_wrecked.glb
!models/trucks/container_blue.glb
!models/trucks/container_red.glb

# Belt-and-suspenders: any other oversized model formats that land in assets.
*.glb.zip

# Safety net: raw editor zips / source bundles sometimes land in assets.
*.zip

# Oversized source audio dropped into assets/Audio/ (added 2026-06-17, each
# ~50-100 MiB — over the 25 MiB cap, and not referenced by the game). Cloudflare
# can't serve a file this large anyway; if this ambience is wanted in-game,
# compress it under 25 MiB or host it in the cloud bucket. Small served SFX in
# this folder (button click.wav, card draw.wav, …) stay under the cap and deploy
# normally, so exclude only the oversized ones by exact name. Files stay on disk.
assets/Audio/Heavy Machines - Factory Ambience.wav
assets/Audio/auction chatter.wav
assets/Audio/fishing.wav
# 73 MiB main-menu music WAV dropped 2026-06-18 — not referenced by index.html and
# over the cap. To use it in-game, compress to MP3/OGG well under 25 MiB and load
# that instead. File stays on disk.
assets/Audio/Main menu music.wav

# Oversized animated unit frame dropped 2026-07-23 (113 MiB — 4.5× over the 25 MiB
# cap; a single oversized file aborts the ENTIRE deploy). Animated-GIF unit frames
# must be compressed/resized under 25 MiB (or converted to a sprite sheet) before
# they can ship. Small GIFs under the cap still deploy normally, so exclude only
# this one by exact name. File stays on disk.
assets/Units/unit frames/New units/Grey Dragon Animate rare.gif

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ✅ COMPRESSED RUNTIME MODELS — re-included 2026-08-19.
# The blanket `**/*.glb` above STAYS. It is the guard that stopped an oversized
# drop aborting the entire deploy (see the header), and removing it would just
# wait for the next 70 MiB model to freeze production again. Instead each model
# that has been through `gltf-transform optimize --compress draco` and VERIFIED
# under the 25 MiB cap is re-included BY NAME below.
#
# Uncompressed masters live in `assets-source/glb-masters/` (outside the deploy
# root, byte-verified before any write). To add a model here: compress it,
# confirm `gltf-transform inspect` reports unchanged mesh/material counts,
# confirm it is under 25 MiB, then add one `!` line. Do not relax the blanket.
#
# ⚠ These are DRACO-compressed. Any page that loads one MUST wire a DRACOLoader
# into its GLTFLoader or the load throws. index.html already does; pack-opener
# and ascent-map were wired in the same commit that added these lines.
!assets/Boosterandpacks/Glb/Booster boxes.glb
!assets/Boosterandpacks/Glb/BOU! pack.glb
!assets/gib files/Prince The adam Changer.glb
!assets/gib files/The Tour Guide.glb
!assets/3d models/Man eacthing plant statue.glb
!assets/3d models/packopening shelf.glb
!assets/3d models/cardshelf.glb
!assets/3d models/Bahamut statue.glb
!assets/3d models/Mythci deck.glb
!assets/3d models/Vendor market cash register.glb
!assets/3d models/base chair.glb
!assets/3d models/cindercore.glb
!assets/3d models/abandontank.glb
!assets/3d models/posters/Birth Of Universe 1.glb
!assets/3d models/Base survivor bed.glb
!assets/3d models/sircedric statue.glb
!assets/3d models/prn nodes.glb
!assets/3d models/Battletable.glb
!assets/3d models/ruin house 1.glb

# 🚜 THE WAREHOUSE FORKLIFT. On the allow-list because **/*.glb above blocks
# every model by default and this one has to ship — the warehouse loads it when
# a player owns the tier-4 lifter.
# ⚠ IT IS 1.67 MB, AND THAT IS THE ONLY REASON IT IS ALLOWED. The file Meshy
#   produced was 122 MB and 3,038,154 triangles, which is four times the 25 MiB
#   ceiling that aborts a whole deploy. tools/build-forklift.mjs decimates it to
#   29,202 triangles; re-export from Meshy and you MUST run that script again
#   before the raw file goes anywhere near this folder.
!assets/models/forklift.glb

# EXCEPTION: the four hospital patients (🏥 /src/hospital). Fixtures rather
# than per-owner uploads — the same four looks walk into every player's ward —
# so a Storage bucket the player has never written to cannot serve them.
# 0.5-0.9 MiB each, far under the 25 MiB cap, packed from ~92 MB of raw export.
!models/hospital/patients/pilgrim.glb
!models/hospital/patients/survivor.glb
!models/hospital/patients/wanderer.glb
!models/hospital/patients/denim.glb

# EXCEPTION: the hospital's Front Desk (🏥 /src/hospital/scene.desk.js). A
# fixture every Medical Corporation stands behind, so it cannot depend on a
# Storage bucket the player has never written to. Packed by
# tools/build-intake-desk.mjs from a 115 MiB / 2,990,122-triangle Meshy export
# down to 35,880 triangles and three 1024² WebP textures — 1.81 MiB, 7% of
# the cap. The raw export is 4.6× the cap and would abort the whole deploy:
# it lives in assets-source/glb-masters/, never here. Re-export → re-run the
# script. WebP: every GLTFLoader this game ships supports EXT_texture_webp.
!models/hospital/intake-desk.glb

# EXCEPTION: the Ward Bay's counter and the Ward Cot (🏥 /src/hospital —
# floor.js BAY_MODEL, beds.js BED_MODEL). Fixtures every ward stands and lies
# in. Packed by tools/pack-glb.mjs from 116 MiB / 3,009,198-triangle and
# 118 MiB / 3,040,134-triangle Meshy exports down to 1.87 MiB (36,108 tris)
# and 1.70 MiB (36,480 tris). Masters in assets-source/glb-masters/.
!models/hospital/ward-desk.glb
!models/hospital/ward-bed.glb

# EXCEPTION: four more hospital stations as models (🏥 /src/hospital —
# floor.js WARD_MODEL, VAULT_MODEL, SUPPLY_MODEL, STOCK_MODEL): the Crate
# Intake, Containment Vault, Supply Bench and Dispensary Stockroom. Fixtures
# every Medical Corporation has. Packed by tools/pack-glb.mjs from ~3M-triangle
# / 113-122 MiB Meshy exports to 4.63 MiB (61,342 tris), 1.81 MiB (36,148),
# 3.32 MiB (49,284) and 1.78 MiB (36,278). Masters in assets-source/glb-masters/.
!models/hospital/crate-intake.glb
!models/hospital/containment-vault.glb
!models/hospital/supply-bench.glb
!models/hospital/dispensary-stockroom.glb

# EXCEPTION: the Compounding Lab and the Loading Dock (🏥 floor.js
# COMPOUND_MODEL, DOCK_MODEL). Same pipeline: tools/pack-glb.mjs from
# 114 MiB / 3,047,710-triangle and 130 MiB / 3,052,710-triangle Meshy
# exports; the lab lands at 1.63 MiB (36,572 tris). The dock's grated deck
# hit meshopt's topology floor (~101k tris at ANY error bound) and went
# through the sloppy simplifier instead — 0.97 MiB, 37,178 tris; its sidecar
# says `simplify: sloppy` so nobody mistakes that for the default pass.
!models/hospital/compounding-lab.glb
!models/hospital/loading-dock.glb

# EXCEPTION: the four city-builder civilians (🚶 node-city agentMesh + /src/crowd).
# Fixtures every city's streets walk with — never per-owner uploads — so a Storage
# bucket the player has never written to cannot serve them. Meshy walking exports
# with one skin and one clip each; the geometry was already ~3,100 triangles, so
# only the textures were packed (tools/glb-textures.mjs → 512 WebP): 335-385 KiB
# each, two orders of magnitude under the 25 MiB cap.
!models/civilians/regal.glb
!models/civilians/survivor.glb
!models/civilians/pilgrim.glb
!models/civilians/wanderer.glb
